 California sanctioned plaintiff's counsel James Dal Bon in Buchanan v. Vuori Inc. (Case 5:23-cv-01121-NC) for filing AI-generated case law citations in a motion for preliminary approval of a wage and hour class action settlement. Dal Bon used six different AI tools to prepare the memorandum, which contained hallucinated quotes and a nonexistent case citation. After the court flagged the fabricated citations, his corrected filing still contained AI-hallucinated case law. The sanctions delayed the class action settlement, ultimately converting it to an individual settlement that abandoned the class members the attorney was supposed to represent.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-03-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Vibe Graveyard\",\"url\":\"https://vibegraveyard.ai/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Vibe Graveyard\",\"url\":\"https://vibegraveyard.ai\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://vibegraveyard.ai/vibe-graveyard-logo.png\"}},\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://vibegraveyard.ai/story/ndcal-dal-bon-ai-citation-class-action-sanctions/\",\"image\":\"https://vibegraveyard.ai/story/ndcal-dal-bon-ai-citation-class-action-sanctions/opengraph-image.png\",\"keywords\":[\"ai-hallucination\",\"legal-risk\",\"vibe-lawyering\",\"ai-assistant\"],\"citation\":[\"https://blogs.duanemorris.com/classactiondefense/2026/02/03/ai-hallucinated-case-citations-prompt-sanctions-and-delay-class-action-settlement/\",\"https://www.law.berkeley.edu/wp-content/uploads/archive/2025/12/Buchanan.pdf\"]}19:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$20\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"posit